\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qc\kerning2\ul\b\f0\fs44\lang16393 Transformer Architecture Basics\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl360\slmult1\qj\ulnone\b0\f1\fs24 A \b Transformer\b0  is a deep learning architecture that uses \b self-attention mechanisms\b0  instead of recurrence (RNNs) or convolutions (CNNs) to process sequences. It was introduced in the 2017 paper \b "Attention Is All You Need"\b0  and forms the foundation of GPT, BERT, ChatGPT, Copilot, Gemini, DALL\'b7E, Codex, and many other AI systems.\par
Instead of processing words one after another, a Transformer processes \b all words simultaneously\b0  and learns which words are important to each other using \b Attention\b0 .\par
\ul\b Architecture\par
\ulnone\b0 A \b Transformer\b0  is a neural network architecture designed to process and understand sequential data such as text, code, audio, and images. It was introduced in 2017 and became the foundation of modern AI models like GPT, BERT, ChatGPT, Copilot, and Gemini.\par
The main goal of a Transformer is to understand the relationship between different words in a sentence, regardless of how far apart those words are. Unlike older models such as Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs), which process one word at a time, Transformers process all words simultaneously. This makes them much faster and more efficient.\par
\b 1. Input Embeddings\par
\b0 Converts words into numerical vectors that the model can understand.\par
\b 2. Positional Encoding\par
\b0 Adds word-order information because Transformers process all words in parallel.\par
\b 3. Self-Attention\par
\b0 Allows each word to focus on important words in the sentence.\par
Example:\par
"The cat drank milk because it was hungry."\par
The model learns that \b "it" refers to "cat"\b0 .\par
\b 4. Multi-Head Attention\par
\b0 Uses multiple attention layers to capture different relationships such as grammar, meaning, and context simultaneously.\par
\b 5. Feed Forward Network (FFN)\par
\b0 Processes attention outputs and learns deeper patterns from the data.\par
\b 6. Add & Layer Normalization\par
\b0 Improves training stability and helps deep networks learn efficiently.\par
