\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj\ulnone\b0\fs24 Tokenization is the process of breaking text into smaller units called tokens. These tokens can be words, subwords, characters, or symbols. Each token is converted into a numerical ID that AI models can understand. Tokenization helps reduce complexity and improves processing efficiency. It is the first step in Transformer-based models such as GPT, BERT, and ChatGPT.\par
\par
Example:\par
Input:\par
"I love Artificial Intelligence!"\par
\par
After Tokenization:\par
["I", "love", "Artificial", "Intelligence", "!"]\par
\par
These tokens are then converted into IDs:\par
"I"            \f5\u8594?\f1\lang16393  101\par
"love"         \f5\u8594?\f1\lang16393  205\par
"Artificial"   \f5\u8594?\f1\lang16393  567\par
"Intelligence" \f5\u8594?\f1\lang16393  890\par
"!"            \f5\u8594?\f1\lang16393  45\par
\par
The AI model processes these numbers instead of the original text.\par
\par
\ul\b\fs28 Importance:\par
\ulnone\b0\fs24 Pretraining is the first stage in training a Generative AI model, where it learns general knowledge from massive datasets such as books, websites, research articles, and code repositories. During this phase, the model learns language structure, grammar, facts, reasoning patterns, and relationships between words by performing tasks like predicting the next word in a sentence. The training process involves analyzing billions of text examples and continuously adjusting model parameters to improve accuracy. Pretraining requires significant computational resources, large amounts of data, and extensive training time. The result is a foundation model such as GPT or BERT, which can later be fine-tuned for specific tasks or domains.\par
\par
\ul\b\fs28 Types of Tokenization\par
\ulnone\fs24 1. Word Tokenization\par
\b0 It splits the text into individual words.\par

\pard\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj\f3\fs20\'b7\tab\f1\fs24 Separates text based on spaces\par
\f3\fs20\'b7\tab\f1\fs24 Each word is treated as one unit\par
\f3\fs20\'b7\tab\f1\fs24 Does not break words further\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj\b 2. Sentence Tokenization\par
\b0 This splits the text into individual sentences.\par

\pard\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj\f3\fs20\'b7\tab\f1\fs24 Breaks text using punctuation (like . ? !)\par
\f3\fs20\'b7\tab\f1\fs24 Helps in dividing large text into smaller parts\par
\f3\fs20\'b7\tab\f1\fs24 Useful for summarization and analysis\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj\b 3. Subword Tokenization\par
\b0 It works by splitting words into smaller meaningful parts.\par

\pard\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj\f3\fs20\'b7\tab\f1\fs24 Breaks long or complex words into smaller pieces\par
\f3\fs20\'b7\tab\f1\fs24 Helps handle unknown words\par
\f3\fs20\'b7\tab\f1\fs24 Balances word and character levels\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj\b 4. Character Tokenization\par
\b0 It splits text into individual characters instead of words.\par

\pard\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj\f3\fs20\'b7\tab\f1\fs24 Breaks every word into letters\par
\f3\fs20\'b7\tab\f1\fs24 Works the same for all languages\par
\f3\fs20\'b7\tab\f1\fs24 Does not depend on words or vocabulary\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj\b 5. N-gram Tokenization\par
\b0 This splits text into groups of consecutive words.\par

\pard\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj\f3\fs20\'b7\tab\f1\fs24 Groups words together instead of splitting them alone\par
\f3\fs20\'b7\tab\f1\fs24 Helps capture relationships between words\par
\f3\fs20\'b7\tab\f1\fs24 Can be bigrams (2 words), trigrams (3 words), etc.\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj\b 6. Byte Pair Encoding (BPE)\par
\b0 Byte Pair Encoding is a subword tokenization technique that splits words into frequently occurring character sequences.\par

\pard\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj\f3\fs20\'b7\tab\f1\fs24 Merges the most frequent pairs of characters or subwords\par
\f3\fs20\'b7\tab\f1\fs24 Reduces vocabulary size while preserving meaning\par
\f3\fs20\'b7\tab\f1\fs24 Widely used in modern NLP models\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj\par

